From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:57:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(codex-native): let Codex apply its own Plan and Default
 mode instructions

Toggling Plan mode, and starting a Default-mode implementation turn,
sent the configured developer_instructions as the collaboration mode's
developer_instructions. Codex's app-server treats that field as the
mode's instructions: a null is filled with the built-in Plan or Default
preset (normalize_collaboration_mode, present since 0.129), and any
value replaces it. The configured developer_instructions are a separate
session setting that these updates never touch. Echoing them therefore
dropped Plan mode's planning instructions for every agent with authored
instructions and repeated the authored text in the mode section.

Send null so Codex applies its preset; authored instructions keep
reaching Codex through config.toml. The unreadable-config guard on the
Plan toggle only protected the echoed value, so it is removed.

Not upstream yet: a candidate for its own upstream PR; drop this copy
once an equivalent fix lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (fix: Codex keeps its built-in Plan and Default mode instructions; no setting)
